    {
      "kind": "supporting_motion_grouping",
      "cause": "raised preparation followed by a stronger reverse sweep did not satisfy the former low-terminal-hand rule",
      "behavior": "retain raised preparation as supporting context only when held high into the later swing and no independent reset is observed; keep two real strokes with a lower reset separate"
    },
    {
      "kind": "motion_peak_search",
      "cause": "the candidate crossing can occur in recovery, clipping the earlier actual motion peak despite its presence in validated context",
      "behavior": "search the existing continuous source context; a sustained 250 ms quiet reset prevents an earlier independent peak from stealing the next action"
    },
    {
      "kind": "ambiguous_phase_rejection",
      "cause": "without independent hitting-side racket support, one hand can pause while the other performs a strong independent sweep",
      "behavior": "retain candidate but mark all phases unavailable with exact source-bound ambiguity reason; never use legacy stage fallback; two separated-frame votes at 3:1 dominance can retain the supported wrist chronology without changing the eight-vote stroke-classification gate"
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This is not an independent blind accuracy benchmark. Engineering sequence rules changed; scoring curves and weights did not.",
    "Original white 5.8 s and ordinary B 34.5 s also become phase-ambiguous because the candidate wrist is unsupported or ownership votes conflict. These are real actions with unresolved model phase attribution, not eliminated false actions.",
    "Existing minimum candidate peak spacing can still merge very fast repeated strokes. Fully off-axis movements may remain review-only.",
    "Final assessment counts and source audit of all 33 records are delegated to the root release-v2 replay."
